document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<p class="note">The diagram groups actual worker calls, local-first transcript mirroring, external adapter operations and store-backed resume. Numbered steps group teaching scenarios rather than one required universal sequence.</p><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen source-linked session workflow steps"></div>'+walk)

reference=[('Real boundary of this demo', 'Two worker processes with isolated SDK config directories simulate host changes on one computer, using the same cwd. The backing adapter is a local file store outside those configs. No remote containers or cloud services are claimed.'), ('Local-first and temporary copies', 'Fresh queries leave a local JSONL until this lab cleans up. Store-backed resumes materialize history into SDK-managed temporary configuration and clean that materialized copy at run end. External mirroring does not mirror general project files.'), ('Ordering and retry rules', 'Persist entries as opaque JSON values, in order. Stable UUIDs are deduplicated to make retries idempotent; metadata without UUIDs stays append-only. This adapter serializes one instance, not concurrent processes.'), ('Production adapters', 'S3 reference adapters store ordered JSONL parts. Redis uses lists and a session index. Postgres stores ordered JSONB rows. Copy and adapt official examples; use transactions/CAS for multiple writers, secure credentials, encryption and retention controls.'), ('Optional methods', 'listSessions enables continue. listSessionSummaries uses incremental SDK folds to avoid loading every transcript for metadata. delete cascades from the main key to subkeys. listSubkeys discovers subagent namespaces; this lab does not invoke subagents.'), ('Failure is observable', 'An injected append outage produces actual native mirror_error messages. The model can still finish using local history. A missing store can fall back to local storage; the missing experiment deliberately has a clean target configuration, then starts a healthy fresh session.'), ('Validation and lifetime', 'The file adapter passes Anthropic’s official 13-contract suite adapted only to Node’s test runner. Additional tests cover UUID retries and overlapping calls. In-memory state dies with the process; the file store is durable across workers but deliberately removed after each classroom experiment.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 41 · Persisting sessions to external storage\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson41-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson41-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson41-session-storage`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3141 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK session storage documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/session-storage)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for official adapter contracts, UUID retries, ordering, workspace and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 41 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')

(PUBLIC/"style.css").write_text((PUBLIC/"style.css").read_text(encoding="utf-8")+'\n#conversation{max-height:540px;overflow:auto}.markdown-body{font-size:22px;line-height:1.6}.markdown-body article,#conversation article{padding:16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.json-view{max-height:380px}#result-history td{max-width:380px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.table{max-height:350px;overflow:auto}#branch-cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,300px),1fr))}#branch-cards .branch-card{padding:20px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#branch-cards .meta{font-size:20px}#session-picker{font-size:21px}#picker-panel .meta{margin-bottom:0}\n',encoding="utf-8")

(APP/"README.md").write_text((APP/"README.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")+'\n\n## Reference backend integrations\n\nThis app runs a single-writer file adapter and two local worker configurations. It does not deploy cloud services. The SDK provides reference adapters to study and adapt:\n\n- [S3: ordered JSONL parts](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/tree/main/examples/session-stores/s3)\n- [Redis: transcript lists and session index](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/tree/main/examples/session-stores/redis)\n- [Postgres: ordered JSONB rows](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/tree/main/examples/session-stores/postgres)\n\nUse the same working directory/project key across workers. For concurrent writers use backend transactions or compare-and-swap; the classroom file adapter serializes only one instance.\n',encoding="utf-8")
